# `@[vectorize]` on a loop the backend can honour: a range loop whose iterations are
# independent (no name written from outside, no I/O). The loop is tagged
# `narval.vectorize` and its body block becomes `vectorized.body`, and an unboxed
# element op in it is what LLVM/linalg turns into SIMD — a body that reaches the runtime
# per element is refused instead (see the other three cases).
# Expected:
# ok

@[vectorize]
for i in 0..3 {
    n = i * 2;
}

write("ok");
